    exampleHands: [
      'Setup example: 5 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: Each hand has four phases: (1) Poker—ante, deal 5 face-up, best hand wins pot; (2) Bingo—dealer calls ranks, players put coins on matching cards, first with all five covered wins coins on cards; (3) Put and Take—dealer turns 10 then 10 cards, players put then take coins by rank; (4) Count-Up—dealer turns 13 cards counting ace to king, players pay dealer when rank matches position. Deal passes left after each hand.',
      "Turn-flow example: Everyone antes. Dealer shuffles and deals 5 cards face up to each player. Best poker hand wins the pot (ties share). Same five cards stay; dealer turns undealt cards one by one calling rank; players with that rank put a coin on each matching card; first to have a coin on all five calls Bingo and wins all coins on everyone's cards. Phase 3: dealer discards own hand and called cards; turns 10 cards—players put 1, 2, … 10 coins per match into pot; then 10 more—players take 1, 2, … 10 per match; remainder to dealer. Phase 4: dealer deals 13 face-up counting ace to king; when turned rank matches count, everyone pays dealer that many coins (J=11, Q=12, K=13). Hand over; next player deals.",
